-- exit: 1
-- The text of a panic is the program's, the report is silt's: control
-- characters in it (a carriage return, an escape sequence, a tab) are
-- shown as escapes, as silt's other messages show a value, so the report
-- cannot move the cursor or colour the terminal. Its line ends stay: the
-- lines after the first are a note. What the program prints itself is
-- not touched.
fn main() {
  println("printed \u{1b}[1mas written\u{1b}[0m")
  panic("a\rb\u{1b}[31mred\nnext\tcolumn")
}
